From: T <t@d.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:55:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 1 + most of Phase 2/3 of the post-scan remediation. D0:
 S5B now runs the per-direction greedy/CELF search over the candidate pool
 under the lookahead-2 stopping rule, subject to the constraint references it
 already computed correctly, and emits selected_book.csv; S8 scores that
 artifact and the old hardcoded top-50-by-worst-day sort is demoted to
 _baseline_top50_sort, written as an explicitly labelled baseline contender so
 the sort-vs-selection delta stays visible. D1: ingest_f0 is skipped when the
 chunked path already collated F0, with a per-family count == collated count
 assertion that aborts on mismatch, so the H.1 trial count is no longer
 doubled. D5: tolerances widened to (1,5,10,15,20,25,30) so same-bar
 concurrence and hour-scale clusters are both measurable; N is chosen from
 evidence, not in code. D3: funnel_rerun is derived from the pool (exists,
 non-empty, provenance current) instead of the hardcoded False, and
 funnel_detail is generated from that check. D4/D10: per-family chunk
 completeness is printed with the missing indices named before collation, and
 only the missing chunks are re-queued - never a sequential re-search. D6: the
 S2B checkpoint branch is deleted. D8: S3B reads this run's own results tree
 first. D9: the filter denominator was my own grammar-coverage loop shadowing
 the pool frame.

